# Keep the build context small — and, first of all, keep SECRETS OUT OF THE IMAGE.
#
# `.env` holds the operator's real provider keys, the Fly API token, and the GitHub App private key.
# The deployed app reads all of those from Fly's secret vault at runtime, so the file must never
# enter the build context: an ignored file cannot be COPYd in by a later careless edit, which makes
# this a structural guarantee rather than a rule someone has to remember.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Version control + local tooling state.
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.grok
.october

# Build/dependency output that the image rebuilds itself (stage 1 runs `npm ci` + `vite build`,
# stage 2 runs `uv sync`) — copying a host-built tree in would defeat the lockfile pinning and can
# carry host-arch binaries into a linux image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Test + local-run artefacts the server never reads.
backend/tests
frontend/e2e
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results
.tvashtr_clones
scripts

# Docs — they change constantly and would bust the build cache for no reason.
*.md
design
prompts
docs
